INT. COURTHOUSE PARKING GARAGE - LEVEL P3 - DAWN

Concrete. Sodium light. One sedan, engine ticking.

LENORE VASQUITH (40s, charcoal suit, burner-thin patience) leans on the driver's door, phone pressed to her ear. In the passenger seat, RUFUS AMOAH (30s, borrowed tie, hands gripping his knees) stares at the dashboard.

                    CLERK (V.O.)
                (phone, tinny)
          Judge Barrow moved you to eight-fifteen.

                    LENORE
          Moved me from nine?

                    CLERK (V.O.)
                (phone)
          Prosecution's witness flew in early.

                    LENORE
          Then I want the exhibit list stipulated before we go on the record.

                    CLERK (V.O.)
                (phone)
          Take it up with the judge.

Lenore ends the call. Knocks on the glass. Rufus lowers the window two inches.

                    RUFUS
          That the clerk?

                    LENORE
          We go early. You say nothing. Not "good morning," not "thank you." Nothing.

                    RUFUS
          What if the judge asks me something?

                    LENORE
          Then I object.

                    RUFUS
          And if you can't?

                    LENORE
          Rufus. Look at me.

He does. She does not blink.

                    LENORE (CONT'D)
          I can.
